  "text": "AVES Oncology Group | Austin Veterinary Emergency & Specialty (AVES)\nSkip to Primary Content\nContact Us\nContact Us\nMap\n7501 North Capital of Texas Highway,\nBuilding A,\nAustin,\nTX,\n78731\nCall\n(512) 343-2837\nEmergency\nEmergency\nPhone:\n(512) 343-2837\nAddress:\n7501 North Capital of Texas Highway,\nBuilding A,\nAustin,\nTX,\n78731\nPay Online\nCareers\nAbout Us\nAbout AVES\nOur Team\nCareers\nAngel Fund\nNews & Blog\nServices\nEmergency\nAnesthesiology\nCardiology\nCritical Care\nDiagnostic Imaging\nInternal Medicine\nInterventional Radiology & Endoscopy\nNeurology & Neurosurgery\nAVES Oncology Group\nSurgery & Orthopedics\nView all Services\nPet Owners\nFAQ\nPrescription Refill Form\nPatient Forms\nPay Online\nFinancing\nReferring Veterinarians\nReferral Portal\nReferral Form\nCase Studies\nContinuing Education\nLunch & Learns\nEmergency\nContact Us\nAVES Oncology Group\nCancer is never an easy diagnosis for your pet, and it can be a frightening and stressful experience for the entire family. Fortunately, AVES is home to board-certified veterinary medical and radiation oncologists that collaborate together to develop the best cancer treatment plan for your pet.\nHearing that your pet has cancer can feel overwhelming, but you are not alone. Our compassionate team is here to guide you through every step, with your pet’s comfort and quality of life at the heart of their care.\nOnce a definitive diagnosis has been made, we typically move to a process called staging. While diagnosis tells us\nwhat\ntype of cancer is present, staging helps us understand\nwhere\nit is in the body. This information allows us to tailor the most appropriate treatment plan for your pet.\nStaging may include a combination of advanced tests such as: bloodwork, urine testing, radiographs (x-rays), ultrasounds, CT or MRI imaging, endoscopy, needle aspirates, or biopsies.\nFollowing diagnosis and staging, your AVES oncologist will thoughtfully guide you through a personalized spectrum of treatment options aligned with your family’s wishes for your pet’s cancer care. Most treatment plans include either a single modality or a coordinated combination of surgery, radiation therapy, chemotherapy, and immunotherapy. Whether working with a medical or radiation oncologist, you’ll receive a guided review of each therapeutic option, supported by collaboration with other specialists to create an elevated, comprehensive plan for your pet.\nLearn more:\nMedical Oncology\nRadiation Oncology\nSurgical Oncology\nCollaborative Cancer Care\nAVES is dedicated to a collaborative, team-based model of care, ensuring your pet receives exceptional, personalized treatment. Our oncologists partner seamlessly with specialists across multiple disciplines, guiding advanced diagnostic and therapeutic decisions tailored to each cancer patient.\nSurgery\nAnesthesiology\nInterventional Radiology\nInternal Medicine\nDiagnostic Imaging\nNeurology\nCardiology\nCritical Care\nComing Soon - Rehabilitation & Acupuncture\nOur Oncology Team\nChristopher Dolan\nDVM, DACVIM\nView Profile\nTimothy Stein\nDVM, PhD, DACVIM\nView Profile\nLauren Smith-Oskrochi\nDVM, DAVCR (RO)\nView Profile\nMichael Deveau\nDVM, DAVCR (RO)\nView Profile\nChristopher Dolan\nDVM, DACVIM\nView Profile\nTimothy Stein\nDVM, PhD, DACVIM\nView Profile\nLauren Smith-Oskrochi\nDVM, DAVCR (RO)\nView Profile\nMichael Deveau\nDVM, DAVCR (RO)\nView Profile\nDepartment Information\nOur Oncology service is open Monday – Friday, 8:00 am – 6:00 pm.\nPlease contact our office at\n(512) 343-2837\nfor more information or to schedule an appointment with our Oncologist.\nContact Us\nAbout AVES\nView all Services\nPatient Forms\nReferral Portal\nContact Us\nPhone:\n(512) 343-2837\nFax:\n(512) 343-2844\nAddress:\n7501 North Capital of Texas Highway\nBuilding A\nAustin\n,\nTX\n78731\nHours of Operation\nMain Hours\nMon\nOpen 24 hrs\nTue\nOpen 24 hrs\nWed\nOpen 24 hrs\nThu\nOpen 24 hrs\nFri\nOpen 24 hrs\nSat\nOpen 24 hrs\nSun\nOpen 24 hrs\nOpen 24/7/365 for Pet Emergencies, Specialty Services Available by Appointment Only.\n©\nCopyright\n2026\nAccessibility\nPrivacy Policy\nTerms & Conditions\nCookie Preferences",
